  "narrative": {
    "intro": "L3HARRIS Global Communications made $458M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. L3HARRIS Global Communications received 89 awards so far, with an average award size of $5.1M. L3HARRIS Global Communications obligations are down 43.0% year over year. The Department of Defense obligated $458M with L3HARRIS Global Communications in FY2026 to date, while the Department of Homeland Security obligated $37.7K and the Department of the Interior obligated $0. Other Communications Equipment Manufacturing is the largest market for L3HARRIS Global Communications, with $448M in obligations, followed by Radio and Television Broadcasting and Wireless Communications Equipment Manufacturing at $8.7M and Fluid Power Cylinder and Actuator Manufacturing at $1.3M. Fiscal-year comparisons show past totals of $468M in FY21, $617M in FY22, $617M in FY23, $1B in FY24, and $803M in FY25. Current-year totals are partial because FY2026 is fiscal year to date. This snapshot focuses on contract obligations and the top buying agencies and NAICS markets for L3HARRIS Global Communications in FY2026 to date.",
